---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import earthriseImg from '../../../assets/posts/earthrise.jpg';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Earthrise">
	<main>
		<nav><a href={base}>&larr; Home</a></nav>
		<h1>Earthrise</h1>
		<img class="post-image" src={earthriseImg.src} alt="Earthrise, photographed from lunar orbit by the Apollo 8 crew" />
		<figcaption>William Anders / NASA, Apollo 8, December 24, 1968. Public domain.</figcaption>
		<p>
			Taken by astronaut William Anders as Apollo 8 emerged from behind the Moon,
			this photograph is often credited with shifting public perception of Earth
			as a single, bounded system rather than an endless backdrop.
		</p>
		<p>
			That shift in scale rhymes with an aerial view taken much closer to home:
			<a href={`${base}posts/grand-prismatic/`}>Grand Prismatic Spring</a>, where
			distance turns a hot spring into an abstract pattern of color.
		</p>
		<p>
			For a wave-scale view of nature's power from the ground, see
			<a href={`${base}posts/great-wave/`}>The Great Wave off Kanagawa</a>.
		</p>
	</main>
</Layout>
